# One line-ending convention, so a file edited from Windows does not come back
# as a whole-file diff.
#
# This repository is edited from a Windows desktop over a Samba share and run
# on a Raspberry Pi, and it had no rule: 35 committed files used CRLF and 53
# used LF, with no pattern.  Any tool that rewrote a file changed its endings
# and turned a six-line edit into a fifteen-hundred-line diff, which happened
# repeatedly and hid the real change each time.
#
# LF everywhere, normalised on commit, checked out as LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.npz binary
*.ico binary
